  <title id="bdl31depthpathology-title">Prior function samples of tanh networks of depth 2, 4 and 8 compared with Gaussian process prior samples</title>
  <desc id="bdl31depthpathology-desc">Top row: fourteen sample functions each from fully connected tanh networks with 2, 4 and 8 layers and fan-in-scaled unit-variance Gaussian weights, on inputs from minus 15 to 15, with a dashed zero mean and a shaded band of two standard deviations. With 2 layers the functions are flat away from the origin and change sharply near it; with 4 layers they change less; with 8 layers they are nearly constant lines. Bottom row: fourteen samples from Gaussian process priors with an RBF kernel (smooth wiggles) and a Matern 3/2 kernel (rougher wiggles), both with unit marginal variance, a dashed zero mean and a shaded band from minus 2 to 2.</desc>
